// LB+datas+plain -- load buffering through data dependencies over plain
// accesses, the out-of-thin-air shape.
//
// Java Access Modes (Bender & Palsberg, OOPSLA 2019), the herd model of their
// Appendix A. Causality, acyclic((po | rf) & opq), covers opaque and stronger
// accesses only: the paper does not tackle thin air for plain accesses, so JAM
// allows it. Over opaque accesses the same shape is forbidden. herd7 cannot
// test this: it never makes a value out of a circular dependency.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r1 := x.load(na);
  y.store(r1, na)
} ||| {
  r2 := y.load(na);
  x.store(r2, na)
}
%%
allow (r1 = 42 && r2 = 42) [JAM]
